1. a default message via super
   raise AppError                  -> "the application failed"
   raise AppError, "given instead" -> "given instead"
2. extra attributes
   NotFound: "not found", code 404
   NotFound: "no such user", code 410
3. overriding message
   e.message "LOUD: x"   e.to_s "x"
4. a family is caught by its base class
   rescue AppError caught AppError
   rescue AppError caught NotFound
   rescue AppError caught Loud
5. full_message, first line (line number masked)
   custom_exception_classes_rb.rb:LINE:in 'Object#boom': gone (NotFound)
6. raise obj calls obj.exception: any object can be raised that way
   raise Ticket.new(7)                -> NotFound: "ticket 7 is missing"
   raise Ticket.new(7), "custom text" -> NotFound: "custom text"
7. detailed_message (3.2) is what full_message prints; message is untouched
   e.message           "bad setting"
   e.detailed_message  "bad setting (Detailed) [hint: check the config]"
   full_message line 1 custom_exception_classes_rb.rb:LINE:in '<main>': bad setting (Detailed) [hint: check the config]
8. initialize without super: the message falls back to the class name
   NoSuper: "NoSuper"
9. == compares class, message and backtrace
   AppError.new("a") == AppError.new("a")  true
   AppError.new("a") == AppError.new("b")  false
10. no exception groups: collect the errors and raise one wrapper
   3 errors: [ArgumentError, TypeError, ArgumentError]
   ArgumentErrors inside: 2, TypeErrors: 1
